
1) Check out this repo on the hadoop master.

2) Install build tools:

apt install gcc maven

3) ./tpch-build.sh

4) Generate data:

tpch-setup.sh was broken down into four scripts, to help debug failures:

./tpch/generate.sh $SCALE
./tpch/load-text.sh $SCALE
./tpch/load-orc.sh $SCALE
./tpch/compute-stats.sh $SCALE

At the end, per-table directories with files in ORC format should be available here:

$ hdfs dfs -ls -C /user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/customer
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/lineitem
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/nation
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/orders
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/part
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/partsupp
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/region
/user/hive/warehouse/tpch_flat_orc_200.db/supplier

To check statistics:
$ sudo -u postgres psql
postgres=# \c metastore
metastore=# \d "TAB_COL_STATS";
metastore=# select * from "TAB_COL_STATS";

Alternatively, take scale=200 data in ORC format from an S3 bucket tpch1:
https://console.yandex.cloud/folders/b1gc52165f3897s3clvr/storage/buckets/tpch1

and find how to import it into Hive. Still need to run the statistics step tpch/compute-stats.sh

== S3 ==

To work with S3, install and configure S3cmd:
https://yandex.cloud/en/docs/storage/tools/s3cmd

Create a bucket, and configure "Access policy" to allow PutObject:
Potentially it is also necessary to configure "Access rights"

See screenshots
https://gist.github.com/alephonea/f36ee19b91c8c662b100d1e692c680ab
